Tokenization in NLP is a process of breaking down text into chunks of words or symbols, known as tokens. Tokenization is an essential step in NLP as it separates words and symbols from each other, which becomes a raw linguistic unit that can be further processed.Tokenization is the critical first step in various NLP tasks, including text classification, sentiment analysis, named entity recognition, etc.

NLP uses a lot of predictive and statistical models that rely on data to be in a format they can work with that is numerical.Tokenization allows NLP to pre-process given text to get the desired result by breaking down the text. It also has to break them down based on the particular NLP pre-processing activity used. Emoticons and emojis in the text can also be tokenized using NLP.

Below are some of the ways used by NLP during tokenization-

- Word tokenization: The tokenization of words in a sentence.
- N-gram tokenization: It is a method used where the length of “n” in a word is to be specified for tokenization. The length of `'n'` can be greater than one or a unigram of length 1.
- Byte Pair Encoding: This helps in encoding rare characters into subword units consisting of multiple bytes of one or more characters.

Additionally, tokenization can be Levenshtein distance, Mallet’s implementation, etc. Breaking word tokenization and sentence splitting are further divided into parts, depending on the context. Typically, tokenization is carried out based on the task’s context to yield an accurate and desirable result.

