- In-Document summarization, the task of summarizing or getting to the crux of a topic – tokenization is an important part of NLU. As it involves breaking down information into subunits and carrying out tasks using them.
- In named entity recognition, tokenization is used to identify the keywords or proper nouns in the text and predict what could be the possible entities matching the words in a document before they can be classified or tagged accurately.
- Also in sentiment analysis, where the primary task is to find any positive or negative sentiment in a sentence, a lot of work starts with tokenization and lemmatization, as it becomes easy to apply the task to each word and make the task more straightforward.
- Chatbots and personal assistants, automated voice services, etc. cannot function without NLP, and most importantly, without tokenization – as understanding the words of user queries is a must before the answer can be detected.
