How are floating-point tensors and fixed-point tensors different?

In short, floating-point tensors are more accurate. The advantage of floating-point tensors is that they can represent a continuous range of values (from negative infinity to positive infinity). In Python, floating-point tensors are often converted to fixed-point tensors, as they can be treated as such, and there are no accuracy issues.

Other languages, such as C, C++, C# or Java, do not have floating point tensors, and fixed-point tensors are used to represent a range of values. This is the type of tensor used in most programming languages, including Python.

