Streaming inference includes several types of analytical software components that produce a database containing a series of decisions made after processing a stream of data.

In live data streams, such as a stream of tweets about a brand, historical data about a rare illness obtained from a health monitoring system, and IoT sensor data that indicates potential mechanical failures in a manufacturing process, examples of streaming analytics and inference can be observed.

