Time series is a very popular application of sequence-to-sequence models, as mentioned before. But generally, time-series prediction only focuses on one fixed target; that is, one may train a model to predict the stock price only for future steps. Sequence generation can predict the entire stock price movement for future steps. In other words, sequence generation considers the whole (longer) picture of the problem.

