A positional encoding is a vector. That vector is added to a word embedding before the creation of attention weights. The result vector - the word as represented by a word embedding AND a positional encoding - moves to the softmax layer where attention weights are created.

This means that:

- attention weights are not biased based on the position of the word
- only the arguments to an attention weight calculation are biased based on the position of the word

